==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|inf=to [[end]] [[up]]|ends up|ending up|ended up|ended up}}

# {{context|idiomatic; with the preposition [[with]]}} To [[conclude]], [[turn out]], sometimes unexpectedly.
#: ''How did things '''end up''' with you and the bricklayer?'' &mdash; ''Great. We got married!''
# {{idiomatic}} To [[arrive]] at a destination, sometimes unexpectedly.
#: ''I was going for a stroll, and '''ended up''' in Slovakia.''
# {{context|of a set of events}} To [[eventually]] [[do]]
#: ''We spent a long time looking for a cheaper deal, but we '''ended up''' buying from the first dealer we met.''

